# `nextMessage` is not a language word: the mail receiver is `receiveMessage`
# (LMX_blog/2026-09-24.md). An unknown head keeps the construction of a named
# Structure with its written contents and executes nothing, so `nextMessage: m`
# defines one in test; the free name m inside it is never read. Entry 7.
fn: test () int
    nextMessage: m
    return: 0
end: test

int: r test()
int: result 7
if: r != 0
    result: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
